From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: map Rx buffers for device to CPU DMA

edma_rx_alloc_buffer_list() maps the buffers it posts to the Rx fill
ring with DMA_TO_DEVICE, in both the linear and the page mode branch,
while edma_rx_reap() unmaps them with DMA_FROM_DEVICE.  The device
writes these buffers and the CPU reads them, and nothing writes the
mapped region from the CPU between the mapping and the producer index
update, so DMA_FROM_DEVICE is the direction both halves should use.
The lengths already agree: alloc_size less the headroom and NET_IP_ALIGN
on the linear path, PAGE_SIZE on the page path.

Nothing is known to misbehave on this SoC, where the arm64
implementation cleans the buffer on map whichever direction it is given
and invalidates it on unmap.  This is an API correctness fix: dma_debug
reports the map and unmap directions as a mismatch, and on a system
where the device sits behind an IOMMU, dma-iommu derives the mapping
permissions from the direction, so DMA_TO_DEVICE maps the buffer without
device write permission and the device's write faults.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_rx.c
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@ static int edma_rx_alloc_buffer_list(str
 		skb_reserve(skb, EDMA_RX_SKB_HEADROOM + NET_IP_ALIGN);
 
 		if (likely(!page_mode)) {
-			buff_addr = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, dma_map_size, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			buff_addr = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, dma_map_size,
+						   DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
 			if (dma_mapping_error(dev, buff_addr)) {
 				dev_dbg(dev, "edma_context:%pK Unable to dma for non page mode",
 					edma_ctx);
@@ -77,7 +78,7 @@ static int edma_rx_alloc_buffer_list(str
 				break;
 			}
 
-			buff_addr = dma_map_page(dev, pg, 0, PAGE_SIZE, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			buff_addr = dma_map_page(dev, pg, 0, PAGE_SIZE, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
 			if (dma_mapping_error(dev, buff_addr)) {
 				dev_dbg(dev, "edma_context:%pK Mapping error for page mode",
 					edma_ctx);
